window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-08825629d583592f"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"administration\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">管理</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。如需查看文档的 Markdown 版本，可在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>。</p> </blockquote> <p>从工作区身份与访问权限开始。随后，为 ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展中受支持的功能配置本地运行时策略，并了解 Codex Cloud 的使用条件、Platform API 访问权限、插件与连接器，以及已连接系统中的权限。</p> <p>为 ChatGPT、Codex 开发者工具、API、插件和已连接系统设置访问权限与策略边界。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">探索身份验证</a> <a id=\"getting-started\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_2\">入门</h2> <p>规划部署，并了解日常管理工具。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">管理员部署指南</a> — 规划访问权限、指定负责人、配置控制措施并验证部署。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f094a985d5b867ef\">管理员插件</a> — 使用 Admin 插件处理权限、审批和受支持的管理工作流程。 <a id=\"feature-configuration\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_3\">功能配置</h2> <p>选择一项设置任务，然后查看相应的访问权限与安全要求。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46\">配置 dots 权限</a> — 管理 dots 的访问权限、通信、计算机和自定义规则。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=for-workspace-admins\">管理 Space 共享与访问</a> — 控制 Library 共享权限，并帮助成员共享页面。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df\">Sites 管理</a> — 启用 Sites、配置连接，并检查托管、访问控制和数据责任。</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/enterprise/teams#for-workspace-admins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">设置团队与 Team Tasks（需联网）</a> — 设置团队权限、连接共享账户并创建重复任务。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">在 Slack 或 Teams 中设置 @ChatGPT</a> — 查看管理员职责和部署前提条件。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=set-up-a-connection\">设置工作区连接</a> — 准备由公司管理的账户并配置工作区连接。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=how-to-set-up-local-computer-access\">为 Work Cloud 和 dots 启用本地计算机访问</a> — 查看共用策略与兼容性，然后分别为 Work 和 dots 启用本地计算机访问。 <a id=\"identity-and-access\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_4\">身份与访问</h2> <p>管理登录、账户配置、角色和凭据。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">身份验证概览</a> — 比较登录方式、凭据存储方式和强制执行控制。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">群组与账户配置</a> — 比较成员资格的来源并了解群组权限。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-83d4edfaf8cd6445\">动态群组</a> — 根据 SCIM 用户属性规则管理群组成员身份。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-16cf27f48eb09b1c\">用户生命周期管理</a> — 为员工配置账户、更新群组访问权限，并撤销离职用户的凭据。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">角色与工作区权限</a> — 查找工作区、运行时、API、插件和源系统的控制项。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88\">个人访问令牌</a> — 创建和管理用于程序化访问的令牌。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7a5e03044e16c67c\">服务账户</a> — 为自动化工作流程创建和管理工作区身份。 <a id=\"deployment-and-configuration\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_5\">部署与配置</h2> <p>部署应用，并配置更新、运行时设置、远程连接和模型访问权限。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">Windows 应用与 CLI 部署</a> — 在受管理的 Windows 设备上部署 Windows 应用和 Codex CLI。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24c62848a3326493\">管理应用更新</a> — 控制桌面应用更新，并通过设备管理平台部署已批准的版本。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置</a> — 查看 Agent Security 中的全局基线、此功能的策略优先级以及受支持的运行时要求。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-649ffe45719449f8\">Codex 安全手册</a> — 配置并验证企业安全控制，再将其组合起来满足常见安全目标。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f\">远程连接</a> — 在已连接的计算机上启动并控制工作。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7d04f9ab1f4a3eeb\">工作区模型可用性</a> — 分别管理 ChatGPT、ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex、Codex CLI、IDE 扩展、Codex Cloud 和 Platform API 的模型访问权限。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">Amazon Bedrock</a> — 配置受支持的本地客户端，以使用 Bedrock 提供的模型。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80\">Bedrock GovCloud 配置</a> — 在 AWS GovCloud 中配置使用 Amazon Bedrock 的本地 Codex 工作流程。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597\">通过网关使用 ChatGPT 登录</a> — 保留用于模型请求的网关，同时使用 ChatGPT 工作区身份。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">使用 API／提供商凭据</a> — 配置 Codex 客户端以使用组织的模型网关，并验证连接。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">部署网关</a> — 配置模型路由、签发凭据，并通过组织的网关部署 Codex。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">网关兼容性</a> — 检查模型请求、流式传输和工具调用所需的 Responses API 行为。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4\">通过 LiteLLM 使用 Bedrock</a> — 配置 LiteLLM 网关，将 Codex 模型请求路由到 Amazon Bedrock。</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work\">ChatGPT Work</h2> <p>查看 ChatGPT Work 概览和管理参考资料。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-18ad336d66dd572e\">概览</a> — 了解本地和云端执行、Work Cloud 的本地计算机访问、网络控制和数据边界。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-eea2edbcef587cb2\">云端安全</a> — 查看托管执行、已连接账户、访问控制、数据保留和审计可见性。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-54e559ed4245e801\">本地安全</a> — 查看本地执行、设备和浏览器访问、托管策略、数据处理方式以及审计方面的限制。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ba100f6664b7be87\">用量与成本</a> — 了解共享额度、账单影响、支出控制和采用规划。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b498643ba7f3888a\">管理员常见问题</a> — 查看 ChatGPT Work 的访问权限、数据、治理、用量和事件控制措施。 <a id=\"collaboration-and-sharing\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_6\">协作与共享</h2> <p>管理 GPT 的共享和所有权。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-517f08511f57e045\">GPT 与共享</a> — 管理工作区内 GPT 的共享、所有权、已连接应用和第三方操作。 <a id=\"plugins-and-connections\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_7\">插件与连接</h2> <p>控制插件安装、随附技能、连接器提供的能力以及已连接服务的访问权限。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">插件控制</a> — 管理插件可用性、连接器访问与操作权限，以及源系统权限。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">插件管理</a> — 从 GitHub 导入并同步工作区插件。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-160e62101398766a\">技能控制</a> — 比较 ChatGPT 工作区、本地文件系统和插件中的技能控制方式。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97\">将自定义 GPT 迁移为插件</a> — 规划工作区迁移，迁移单个 GPT 或符合条件的批次，并测试和共享替代插件。 <a id=\"usage-and-analytics\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_8\">用量与分析</h2> <p>查看工作区用量和采用情况，并自动生成报告。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">工作区分析</a> — 查看工作区级别的 ChatGPT 采用情况和 Codex 用量。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-474523711974414a\">Usage Insights</a> — 查看 ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 的用量，并与团队一起评估工作流程成效。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a> — 使用 Codex Analytics API 自动生成开发者活动和代码审查报告。 <a id=\"security-and-compliance\"></a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_9\">安全与合规</h2> <p>查看工作区安全策略、治理和审计控制措施。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64\">治理</a> — 针对不同问题选择合适的分析、支出和审计界面。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dccd5924f08b9ad8\">Agent Security</a> — 管理 Global 策略基线，以及受支持的 Local 和 Codex Cloud 环境设置。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c369cec5f3b8338d\">Prisma AIRS</a> — 对 Codex 提示应用工作区级别的安全策略。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b70d1395449a00f1\">HIPAA 配置</a> — 为可能处理受保护健康信息的工作流程配置本地运行时保护措施。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">合规 API 与审计事件</a> — 导出活动记录，用于审计和调查工作流程。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"administration\">Administration</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Start with workspace identity and access. Then configure local runtime policy for supported capabilities in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, and IDE extension; Codex cloud eligibility; Platform API access; plugins and connectors; and permissions in connected systems.</p> <p>Set access and policy boundaries for ChatGPT, Codex developer tools, APIs, plugins, and connected systems.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Explore authentication</a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2> <p>Plan your rollout and explore tools for routine administration.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4\">Admin rollout guide</a> — Plan access, assign owners, configure controls, and verify the rollout.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f094a985d5b867ef\">Admin plugin</a> — Use the Admin plugin for permissions, approvals, and supported administrative workflows.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"feature-configuration\">Feature Configuration</h2> <p>Choose a setup task, then review its access and security requirements.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8b62a89b49b84e46\">Configure dots permissions</a> — Manage dots access, communication, computers, and custom rules.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-418e376165928c0b?anchor=for-workspace-admins\">Manage Space sharing and access</a> — Control Library sharing permissions and help members share pages.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df\">Sites administration</a> — Enable sites, configure connections, and review hosting, access controls, and data responsibilities.</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/enterprise/teams#for-workspace-admins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Set up teams and Team Tasks (online)</a> — Set team permissions, connect shared accounts, and create recurring tasks.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">Set up @ChatGPT in Slack or Teams</a> — Review administrator responsibilities and deployment prerequisites.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d409bf3c6a23c7d1?anchor=set-up-a-connection\">Set up a workspace connection</a> — Prepare company-managed accounts and configure a workspace connection.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d50d47c21e8fd4ad?anchor=how-to-set-up-local-computer-access\">Local computer access for Work Cloud and dots</a> — Review shared policies and compatibility, then enable local computer access separately for Work and dots.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"identity-and-access\">Identity and access</h2> <p>Manage sign-in, provisioning, roles, and credentials.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Authentication overview</a> — Compare sign-in methods, credential storage, and enforcement controls.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10dd8667120ae18c\">Groups and provisioning</a> — Compare membership sources and understand group permissions.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-83d4edfaf8cd6445\">Dynamic groups</a> — Manage group membership with rules based on SCIM user attributes.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-16cf27f48eb09b1c\">User lifecycle management</a> — Provision employees, update group access, and revoke departing users' credentials.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">Roles and workspace permissions</a> — Find workspace, runtime, API, plugin, and source-system controls.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f5bc151215cdfb88\">Personal access tokens</a> — Create and manage tokens for programmatic access.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7a5e03044e16c67c\">Service accounts</a> — Create and manage workspace identities for automated workflows.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"deployment-and-configuration\">Deployment and configuration</h2> <p>Deploy apps and configure updates, runtime settings, remote connections, and model access.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3a9100c321640450\">Windows app and CLI deployment</a> — Deploy the Windows app and Codex CLI on managed Windows devices.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24c62848a3326493\">Manage app updates</a> — Control desktop app updates and deploy approved versions through your device management platform.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a> — Review the global baseline in Agent Security, policy precedence for this feature, and supported runtime requirements.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-649ffe45719449f8\">Codex security cookbook</a> — Configure and verify enterprise security controls, then combine them for common security goals.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f\">Remote connections</a> — Start and control work on connected computers.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7d04f9ab1f4a3eeb\">Workspace model availability</a> — Separate model access for ChatGPT, Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, the IDE extension, Codex cloud, and the Platform API.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-fc9fbba758a53038\">Amazon Bedrock</a> — Configure supported local clients to use models available through Bedrock.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f780ae4c53905f80\">Bedrock GovCloud configuration</a> — Configure local Codex workflows with Amazon Bedrock in AWS GovCloud.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e25dfff3918fe597\">Sign in with ChatGPT through a gateway</a> — Keep your gateway for model requests while using your ChatGPT workspace identity.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-5d0a94de49bd5694\">Use API/provider credentials</a> — Configure one Codex client to use your organization's model gateway and verify the connection.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d8c21044e817c0d5\">Roll out a gateway</a> — Configure model routes, issue credentials, and deploy Codex through your organization’s gateway.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e9de2a6a736ddc26\">Gateway compatibility</a> — Check the Responses API behavior required for model requests, streaming, and tool calls.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-886686d95c8255a4\">Bedrock through LiteLLM</a> — Configure a LiteLLM gateway to route Codex model requests to Amazon Bedrock.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"chatgpt-work\">ChatGPT Work</h2> <p>Review the ChatGPT Work overview and administration reference.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-18ad336d66dd572e\">Overview</a> — Understand local and cloud execution, Local computer access with Work Cloud, network controls, and data boundaries.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-eea2edbcef587cb2\">Cloud security</a> — Review hosted execution, connected accounts, access controls, retention, and audit visibility.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-54e559ed4245e801\">Local security</a> — Review local execution, device and browser access, managed policies, data handling, and audit limitations.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ba100f6664b7be87\">Usage and cost</a> — Understand shared credits, billing impact, spending controls, and adoption planning.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b498643ba7f3888a\">Admin FAQ</a> — Review access, data, governance, usage, and incident controls for ChatGPT Work.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"collaboration-and-sharing\">Collaboration and sharing</h2> <p>Manage GPT sharing and ownership.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-517f08511f57e045\">GPTs and sharing</a> — Manage GPT sharing, ownership, connected apps, and third-party actions across your workspace.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"plugins-and-connections\">Plugins and connections</h2> <p>Control plugin installation, bundled skills, connector-backed capabilities, and connected-service access.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-20bc98306a44b420\">Plugin controls</a> — Manage plugin availability, connector access and actions, and source-system permissions.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ab115ea47731f92a\">Plugin management</a> — Import and sync workspace plugins from GitHub.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-160e62101398766a\">Skill controls</a> — Compare ChatGPT workspace, local filesystem, and plugin skill controls.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-866d18fe9ed30c97\">Migrate custom GPTs to plugins</a> — Plan your workspace transition, migrate individual GPTs or eligible batches, and test and share replacement plugins.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"usage-and-analytics\">Usage and analytics</h2> <p>Review workspace usage and adoption, and automate reporting.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Workspace analytics</a> — Review workspace-level ChatGPT adoption and Codex usage.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-474523711974414a\">Usage Insights</a> — Explore usage across ChatGPT Work and Codex and assess workflow results with your team.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-88b1ced5fbccd242\">Analytics API</a> — Automate developer activity and code review reporting with the Codex Analytics API.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"security-and-compliance\">Security and compliance</h2> <p>Review workspace security policies, governance, and audit controls.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-05f8d80ccc7b0b64\">Governance</a> — Choose the right analytics, spend, and audit surface for each question.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dccd5924f08b9ad8\">Agent security</a> — Manage the Global policy baseline and supported Local and Codex Cloud environment settings.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c369cec5f3b8338d\">Prisma AIRS</a> — Apply workspace-wide security policies to Codex prompts.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b70d1395449a00f1\">HIPAA configuration</a> — Configure local runtime safeguards for workflows that may handle protected health information.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API and audit events</a> — Export activity records for audit and investigation workflows.</li> </ul>"};
